# Source of truth

`docs/source-of-truth.md` is the live inventory of every user-facing function on Stick It Out. `docs/stack.md` is how the hosts, the member screens, and the analyzer fit together. Read both before changing product behavior. `README.md` is the short map other agents see first.

- Read it before changing product behavior.
- Update it in the same turn you add, remove, ship, or break a feature. Status must match what is actually live, not what we planned.
- Do not mark a path `live` if it only works locally, or if it writes somewhere the dashboard does not read.
- Waitlist signups must land in D1 **and** Resend lists (`SIO Waitlist` / `SIO All`). Admin Members reads D1 only. IONOS `leads.json` is a backup, not the dashboard.
- Do not invent Stripe URLs, reviews, or unpublished lessons. Founding rates stay $19.99/mo and $149/yr.

## Finish check (every turn that changes anything)

- Before saying a task is done, reopen `docs/source-of-truth.md` and confirm it matches what you just shipped. If it does not, fix it first.
- When something moves (host, server, tunnel, folder), search the doc for the old place and fix every mention.
- Keep numbered Known gaps items in order, bump "Last updated", and record the newest applied D1 migration and Worker version.
- Never put keys or tokens in the doc or the repo. It is public.
- The full list is in "Rules for keeping this file true" at the top of the doc.
